# What must NOT reach a build context — and therefore must not reach a public
# image on Docker Hub.
#
# The first two entries are the important ones. Everything else is size.

# ---- secrets ----
# Credentials arrive as environment variables at run time (docker-compose.yml
# env_file). A .env copied into a layer is permanent: `docker history` and a
# layer extract will pull it back out, and deleting it in a later RUN does not
# remove it from the layer underneath. Anyone who can pull the image gets it.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
**/.env
mlflow/.env
*.pem
*.key

# ---- your documents ----
# data/raw holds the source PDFs and DOCXs. They are already chunked and
# uploaded to Qdrant, so the serving image has no use for them — and shipping
# someone's corpus inside a public image is its own kind of leak.
data/
!data/raw/.gitkeep
!data/processed/.gitkeep

# ---- evaluation and experiment output ----
mlflow.db
mlflow/mlflow.db
mlflow/mlartifacts/
mlruns/
evaluation/results/
.deepeval/

# ---- notebooks: large, and full of outputs ----
Notebooks/
*.ipynb
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# ---- local environments ----
venv/
.venv/
env/
*.egg-info/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# ---- caches and tooling ----
.git/
.gitignore
.github/
.pytest_cache/
.vscode/
.idea/
logs/
outputs/
tests/
conftest.py
pytest.ini

# ---- docs ----
docs/
*.md
!README.md
